$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-(thiophen-2-ylsulfanyl)quinoline-3-carboxylic acid (7). A
solution of 2.00g(.010mol) 3-carboxyl-2-chloroquinoline, 2.32g (.020mol)
2- thiophenethiol and 5mL acetic acid was stirred and heated at 75°C for
30min. After cooling, the mixture was diluted with 25mL ethyl acetate.
The organic layer was washed three times with 50mL of 5% sodium sulfite,
dried with magnesium sulfate and allowed to concentrate. The solid
obtained was purified by column chromatography with 1:1 ethyl
acetate:hexane with 10% methanol. 2.30g of solid 7 were obtained (80%
yield). mp: decomposition at 173°C. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) 8.97 (s, 1H),
8.10 (d, 1H), 7.85 (d, 1H), 7.79 (d, 1H), 7.60 (m, 2H), 7.39 (d, 1H),
7.20 (t, 1H). 13C NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) 127.4, 129.2, 129.6, 131.7, 132.2,
132.7, 132.9, 134.4, 134.5, 137.4, 140.5, 154.5, 164.9, 171.5. IR (NaCl)
3531, 3005, 1092, 903. Anal. calc. 287.00 m/z ASAP (+ mode) 270.00
(ionizes with loss of carboxyl OH) (C14H9NOS2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
