$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of thioethers 8b-f Potassium
carbonate (85 mg, 0.61 mmol, 1.10 equiv.) was added to a solution of
thiol (1.13 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) and stirred for 15 min at room
temperature. A solution of
9-(2’,3’,5’-tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-2,6-dichloropurine 3 (250 mg,
0.56 mmol, 1 equiv.) in DMF (5 mL) was added and the resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at 35°C (HPLC Control). Then the reaction mixture was
diluted with EtOAc (40 mL) and the organic phase was washed with brine (7
× 25 mL), dried over anh. Na2SO4 and evaporated under reduced pressure.
Silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc; gradient 33%→66%)
provided product.
9-(2’,3’,5’-Tri-O-acetyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-2-chloro-6-(4-bromophenyl)thio-9H-purine
(8e): A white foam. R f = 0.48 (hexane/EtOAc = 1:2). IR (KBr): 2953,
2854, 1748, 1558, 1441, 1372, 1224, 1164, 1092, 1069, 1010; 1H-NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 8.13 (s, 1H, H-C(8)), 7.59 (td, 2H, 3 J = 8.6 Hz, 4
J = 2.7 Hz, Ar), 7.49 (td, 2H, 3 J = 8.6 Hz, 4 J = = 2.7 Hz, Ar), 6.19
(d, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 5.5 Hz, H-C(1’)), 5.79 (t, 1H, 3 J 1'-2' = 3 J 2'-3'
= 5.5 Hz, H-C(2’)), 5.58 (dd, 1H, 3 J 2'-3' = 5.5 Hz, 3 J 3'-4' = 4.3 Hz,
H-C(3’)), 4.45 (q, 1H, 3 J 3'-4' = 3 J 4'-5' = 4.3 Hz, H-C(4’)), 4.40 (d,
1H, 3 J 4'-5' = 0.8 Hz, Ha-C(5’)), 4.39 (d, 1H, 3 J 4'-5b' = 4.3 Hz,
Hb-C(5’)), 2.15, 2.14, 2.08 (3s, 9H, H3COOC-C(2’,3’,5’)); 13C-NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 170.2, 169.5, 169.3, 162.5, 154.1, 150.1, 141.6,
136.8, 132.5, 130.2, 125.3, 124.5, 86.1, 80.7, 73.2, 70.6, 62.9, 20.8,
20.5, 20.3; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C22H21N4O7SBrCl [M+H]+, 598.9997; found
598.9981.
